  "additional_review": [
    "Exact Selected, H, context, finite limits and seven opening options form a concrete implementable contract using the accepted Envelope APIs.",
    "Group intent classification precedes legacy fallback; sanitized valid group states retain selection H for later group-only dropping. Drop is idempotent and legacy/non-group identity is explicit.",
    "Result uses the supported pure completion facade and original handle identity. Late successful open captures original completion before deadline/cancel checks; malformed success emits cleanup-unconfirmed invalid_response without fabricated completion.",
    "Raw cleanup-unconfirmed atom/tuple is discriminated before generic normalization. Transport finish with an unbound completion returns cleanup_unconfirmed and retains the hold in existing source, supporting the specified fail/settle behavior.",
    "Local preparation/gate/expiry uses neutral fail/settle; attempted client failures use existing upstream_fail mapping; original completion and transport/group/service cleanup order remain explicit.",
    "Literal one-clause activation denial must dominate every actual new group open. Actual dispatch, alias threading, timer effects, carrier-to-ready and legacy behavior require later independent code review and fresh scoped execution.",
    "Queued cancellation/DOWN, actual owner/instance association, startup four-root/source overlap, Probe/recovery, admission and numeric accounting remain later obligations; this package cannot activate them."
  ],
